      {
        "name": "Exposure",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "No part of the response body or contact record reaches the log: HTTPError logs only the code and reason phrase, and other failures log only `type(...).__name__`, never `str(e)` (which for JSONDecodeError would include document text); minor residual risk is that an uncaught exception like RemoteDisconnected or IncompleteRead would still produce a bare traceback, though without the body."
      },
      {
        "name": "Diagnosis",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The urlopen/json.load call is inside the try, every handled path exits 1, and the log carries status, reason, and exception type, but it omits a request id (e.g. from `e.headers`, which is safe to log) and an error code, offering the latter only as a follow-up."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The diff touches only the imports and the error handling around the API call, and the agent explicitly left the missing-token and missing-file cases alone while offering to handle them."
      }
